  "description": "Good things don't always come in small packages, the Steel Reserve 1.1 rolls along on a 26\" wheelset made up of XM 260 double wall alloy rims and Kenda K-Rad 2.3\" wide tires. 1.1 is equally at home at the bike park as it is at the dirt jumps thanks to its full crmo frame with internal head tube available in both short and long, and a rigid crmo fork. The fork is suspension corrected which means if you choose to add a suspension fork down the road the overall geometry of the bike does not change-its \"suspension ready\". Steel Reserve 1.1 comes with a 3 pc crmo crankset and a 25/12 gear ratio that's ideally suited for freestyle mtb riding.\nHaro full Crmo Steel Reserve frame w/ internal head tube\n21.8\" TT (Short) & 22.5\" TT (Long)\nRigid Crmo fork, Suspension corrected, w/ disc brake tabs\nHaro Crmo 8 Spline 3-pc crankset, 25t sprocket\nHaro Steel 65mm riser bar w/ Haro Counterfeit grips\nHaro front load BMX stem\nHaro Padded Slim one piece seat/post, 25.4mm O.D.\nWeinmann XM260 alloy DW 36h rims\nPivit alloy disc cassette hub w/ 12t Crmo cog\nKenda K-Rad 26 x 2.3\" tires\nTektro Aries MD-M280 mechanical rear disc brake",
